249
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,697
Do you know who's hosting this tournament?

250
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,980
I have no idea. It's a mystery.

251
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,060
Nobody seems to know.

252
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,917
Everyone I spoke to got
an anonymous invitation.

253
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,537
But there is a buzz going
around that it's someone

254
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:22,800
with a ton of cash and
an obnoxious attitude.

255
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,960
I'd guess Kaiba.

256
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:28,460
That must be why Ishizu told me to enter.

257
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:33,761
If the events of the past are to happen
again, I must face Kaiba in this tournament.

258
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,057
What are you mumbling about?

259
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:40,081
Anyway, nobody knows for sure who
it is that's throwing this thing.

260
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,957
I suppose we'll find out soon.

261
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:44,777
It's pretty safe to say
it's not Pegasus again.

262
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:49,742
Speaking of Pegasus, this is beginning to
look like Duelist Kingdom all over again.

263
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,097
You can say that again.

264
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:54,592
There certainly are a lot of
familiar faces in this crowd.

265
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:57,760
Most of whom I'm not too happy to see.

266
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:00,780
Oh, you're right.

267
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,120
That's Weevil Underwood and Rex Raptor.

268
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:06,940
And over there's Esperoba.

269
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,780
They say he uses psychic powers to duel.

270
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,235
And Mako's here, too.

271
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,498
If what Mai said earlier is correct,

272
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:16,796
then this tournament is going
to have one new wrinkle.

273
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,880
And there he is now.

274
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,310
Taiba.

275
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:23,840
Greetings, duelists.

276
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,060
Welcome to the town of Domino.

277
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:31,417
But more importantly,
welcome to my tournament.

278
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:35,940
I don't know which is bigger, his
ego or his melon on the big screen.

279
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:38,380
Let's hear what Kaiba has to say.

280
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:41,637
I see you each received
your private invite to

281
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,880
Kaiba Corp's very exclusive
Duel Monsters Tournament,

282
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:48,021
and you had enough brains
to show up here tonight.

283
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:49,777
What do you mean, Kaiba?

284
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:52,580
Being that you are all elite duelists,

285
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:56,460
I've added special rules to my
tournament just for experts.

286
00:18:57,120 --> 00:19:01,680
For example, you will duel using
these new improved duel discs.

287
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:03,137
Check that out!

288
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:05,897
Man, that Kaiba Corp's
got the coolest products!

289
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:10,509
Another new rule that I designed for
the tournament is that before each duel,

290
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:13,288
both players must ante
up their rarest card,

291
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:16,872
and the loser of the duel
forfeits his card to the winner.

292
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,680
Forfeit my Dark Magician?

293
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:22,517
That means losing even
one duel can ruin my deck.

294
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:25,697
My competition will make Pegasus and his

295
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:28,368
Duelist Kingdom tournament
look like a joke.

296
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:31,420
Pegasus, it's not you, Kaiba! You're cool!

297
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:34,850
Huh?

298
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,990
Kaiba.

299
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,540
I knew you'd come, Yugi.

300
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:47,840
We'll see which one of us
is the number one duelist.

301
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:53,857
Don't forget to register and
pick up your dual disc Because

302
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:58,140
exactly one week from today My
Battle City tournament begins

303
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,260
You're on, Kaiba

304
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,880
Battle City, eh?

305
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:07,421
That is correct,

306
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:11,874
Master The world's most elite duelists
have assembled for this tournament

307
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:16,637
How very convenient for
us that so many of our

308
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:19,308
targets have gathered
together in one place.

309
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:25,160
Now, my rare hunters, go to the
town of Domino at once! Yes, sir.

310
00:20:26,020 --> 00:20:28,320
It's time to begin the hunt!

311
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:41,750
Domino!
